$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Solvent Procedure Aldehyde 1 (3.0 mmol) and isocyanide 3 (3.3
mmol) were added to the solution of a carboxylic acid 2 (3.3 mmol) in
methylene chloride (3 mL) at room temperature. The reaction mixture was
stirred at ambient temperature for 24 h and then concentrated in vacuo.
The crude product was purified by silica-gel flash chromatography using
hexane/ethyl octane 6:4 as an eluent to afford the corresponding product
4. Compound 4e, yield 90%. 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 1.28 (t. J= 7.1
Hz, 3H), 2.08 (s, 3H), 3.04-3.34 (m, 2H), 3.99 (dd, J = 3.6 Hz, J=5.1 Hz,
2H), 4.21 (q, J= 7.1 Hz, 2H), 5.42 (dd, J= 4.7 Hz, J= 7.5 Hz, 1H), 6.48
(s, 1H), 7.13-7.35 (m, 5H). 13C NMR (50 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 14.7. 21.4,
38.3, 41.6, 62.2, 74.7, 127.5, 128.9, 129.9, 130.0, 136.4, 169.7, 169.9,
171.1. Anal, calcd. for C15H19NO5: C, 61.42; H, 6.53; N, 4.78. Found: C,
61.62; H, 6.64; N, 4.81. HRMS (ESI): m/z calcd. for C15H19NO5Na [M +
Na]+: 316.1161. Found: 316.1155.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Passerini reaction, reaction run without solvent gave lower yield
