$DATUM 67-56-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Aminopyrimidine or
Aminopyridine Derivative Synthesis. To a 1 M solution of carbonyl
compound (1 mmol) in methanol or toluene were added the amine (1.0
equiv), the isocyanide (1.0 equiv), and the hydroxypyrimidine or
hydroxypyridine (1.0 equiv). The resulting mixture was stirred at 60 or
90 °C under an inert atmosphere and concentrated in vacuo. The crude
product was then purified by flash chromatography on silica gel to give
the desired adduct. 2-(N-(4-chloro benzyl)-N-(6-methyl-2-phenyl
pyrimidin-4-yl)amino)-N-cyclohexyl butanamide.White solid. Yield (16h at
60°C in MeOH): 89%. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 8.44-8.38 (m, 2H),
7.54-7.48 (m, 3H), 7.29 (d, 2H, J = 8.6 Hz), 7.20 (d, 2H, J = 8.6 Hz),
6.62 (br s, 1H), 6.10 (s, 1H), 5.26 (br s, 1H), 4.76 (d, 1H, J = 17.2
Hz), 4.68 (d, 1H, J = 17.2 Hz), 3.74-3.63 (m, 1H), 2.40 (s, 3H), 2.21-
2.08 (m, 1H), 1.84-1.66 (m, 2H), 1.63-1.36 (m, 5H), 1.33-1.13 (m, 4H),
0.97 (t, 3H, J = 7.2 Hz). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100.6 MHz) δ 170.2, 166.9,
163.3, 138.6, 138.5, 136.7, 133.4, 130.8, 129.4, 128.9, 128.3, 101.7,
59.8, 49.0, 48.1, 33.1, 32.9, 25.7, 25.0, 24.8, 24.7, 22.3, 11.6. I.R.
(thin film) 3336, 2932, 2855, 1671, 1573, 1480, 1379 cm-1. MS (DI, CI
NH3) m/z 478. HRMS Calcd. for C28H33ClN40 476.2343, Found 476.2349. m.p.
123°C.
