$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure I for the Passerini
Reaction. The reactions were generally carried out at a concentration of
0.70 M of DHPone and 0.77 M of the other two components in CH2Cl2.
Deviations from these concentrations are due to solubility problems and
are reported for every product. The dihydropyridone was dissolved in DCM,
followed by addition of 1.1 equiv of carbonyl compound and 1.1 equiv of
carboxylic acid. After being stirred at rt until completion, the reaction
mixture was concentrated in vacuo and the crude product purified by
column chromatography. The resulting diastereomeric mixture could not be
separated in any case and the diastereomeric ratio was determined via 1H
NMR analysis for all the products with the exception of 7g (HPLC).
Passerini product 7h. According to General Procedure I: Reaction between
dihydropyridone 6f, isobutyraldehyde and phenylacetic acid afforded after
3 days 7h (136 mg, 89%) as a 6:4 mixture of two diastereoisomers as a
pale yellow foam. Column chromatography was performed with c-hexane/EtOAc
8:2. 1H NMR (250 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm) 8.03 (s, 1H, major), 1.97 (s, 1H,
minor), 7.59-7.18 (m, 14H + 14H), 5.73 (d, J = 10.8 Hz, 1H + 1H), 5.62
(d, J = 6.7 Hz, 1H + 1H), 5.05 (d, J = 3.68 Hz, 1H, major), 4.89 (d, J =
4.5 Hz, 1H, minor), 4.68-4.64 (m, 1H + 1H), 3.80 (s, 2H, minor), 3.79 (s,
2H, major), 2.16-1.20 (m, 9H + 9H), 0.85-0.70 (m, 6H + 6H); 13C NMR (63
MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm) 171.8 (C, minor), 171.7 (C, major), 170.2 (C,
minor), 170.0 (C, major), 167.3 (C, major), 167.3 (C, minor), 138.6 (C,
major), 138.4 (C, minor), 135.0 (C, major), 134.9 (C, minor), 134.1 (2 x
C), 133.96 (C), 133.8 (C), 133.4 (C, minor), 133.3 (C, major), 130.3
(CH), 130.0 (2 x CH), 129.4 (CH), 129.3 (CH), 129.2 (CH), 129.1 (CH),
128.9 (CH), 128.8 (CH), 128.6 (CH), 128.5 (CH), 128.4 (CH), 128.1 (CH),
128.0 (CH), 127.1 (2 x CH), 127.0 (CH), 125.1 (CH), 106.5 (CH, minor),
106.3 (CH, major), 104.2 (CH major), 103.6 (CH, minor), 78.5 (CH), 77.5
(CH), 61.1 (C, major), 61.0 (C, minor), 46.9 (CH, minor), 46.4 (CH,
major), 41.4 (CH2, minor), 41.3 (CH2, major), 30.5 (CH), 25.6 (CH2,
minor), 25.4 (CH2, major), 24.1 (CH2, major), 24.0 (CH2, minor), 22.8 (2
x CH2, minor), 21.9 (2 x CH2, minor), 18.7 (CH3, major), 18.6 (CH3,
minor), 16.8 (CH3, minor), 16.3 (CH3, major); IR (NaCl): 2931 (m), 1743
(s), 1670 (s), 1488 (s); HRMS (EI, 70 eV): calculated for C36H38N2O4 (M+)
562.2832, found 562.2827; MS (EI, 70 eV): m/z (%) = 562 (8), 327 (100),
298 (16), 212 (73), 91 (7).
