$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Preparation of
Compounds 6 A mixture of acid 3 (1 mmol), alkyl isocyanide 4 (1 mmol) and
oxo compound 5 (1 mmol) was stirred in 1 ml of [bmim]Br for 3 h at r.t.
Then 5 ml of water was added and the mixture was extracted with Et2O (2 ×
10 ml). The solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure to leave a
residue that was purified by column chromatography (silica gel (230-400
mesh; Merck), hexane/AcOEt 4:1) to afford desired pure products.
3-(Cyclohexylcarbamoyl)-2,4-dimethylpentan-3-yl-2-(3-benzoylthioureido)propanoate
(6d). White powder; yield: 0.42 g (89%). m.p.: 88-89 °C. IR (KBr): ν̃ =
3394, 3313, 3252, 1725, 1644, 1601, 1381, 1176 cm-1. EI-MS: m/z (%) = 475
(M+, 38), 234 (25), 242 (23), 225 (65), 105 (100), 84 (21), 77 (24), 43
(20). Anal. Calcd. for C25H37N3O4S (475.65): C, 63.26; H, 7.84; N, 8.83.
Found: C, 62.82; H, 8.23; N, 9.05. 1H NMR: δ = 0.91 (3H, d, 3J = 6.9,
Me), 0.96 (3H, d, 3J = 6.9, Me), 1.01 (6H, d, 3J 6.9, 2Me), 1.06-1.91
(10H, m, 5CH2), 1.68 (3H, d, 3J = 7.2, Me), 2.12 (2H, septet, 3J = 6.9,
2CH), 3.07 (1H, septet, 3J = 6.9, CH), 3.80 (1H, m, CH), 5.08 (1H,
quintet, 3J = 7.2, CH), 6.63 (1H, d, 3J = 8.1, NH), 7.54 (2H, t, 3J =
7.0, 2CH), 7.66 (1H, t, 3J = 7.0, CH), 7.87 (1H, d, 3J = 7.0, 2CH), 9.11
(1H, s, NH), 11.10 (1H, d, 3J = 7.2, NH). 13C NMR: δ = 16.6 (2Me), 17.8
(2Me), 18.2 (Me), 25.2 (CH2), 25.3 (CH2), 25.9 (CH2), 31.2 (CH), 31.5
(CH), 33.5 (CH2), 33.7 (CH2), 48.6 (CH), 55.6 (CH), 99.1 (C), 127.9
(2CH), 129.6 (2CH), 131.8 (C), 134.2 (CH), 167.2 (C=O), 168.8 (C=O),
169.9 (C=O), 180.5 (C=S).
