$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Experimental Section Representative Procedure for the Passerini Reaction
of α-Mesyloxyketones 2. Compound 9a. To a sample of R-mesyloxyketone 2a
(48 mg, 0.2 mmol) under N2 in a 5 mL round-bottom flask was added acetic
acid (13 μL, 0.22 mmol, 1.1 equiv) and t-butyl isonitrile (25 μL, 0.22
mmol, 1.1 equiv). The resulting homogeneous solution was stirred at rt
under N2 for 20 h. The product was purified by silica gel flash column
chromatography (3:7 EtOAc:hexanes, Rf = 0.2) to afford 9a (68 mg, 88%) as
a pale-yellow oil. IR (CH2Cl2) 3435(s), 2964(s), 1748(s), 1672(s),
1523(s); CIMS (methane) m/z 386 (M+H), 344, 326, 290, 266.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM no solvent, Passerini reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Studies on the Chemistry and Reactivity of α-Substituted Ketones in
Isonitrile-Based Multicomponent Reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
