$DATUM 75-09-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a 1 dram glass vial containing
dichloromethane (.25 mL), oxo-compound (.5 mmol), (S)-Boc-Pro-OH (.5
mmol, 107.6mg), and isocyanoacetate derived from (S)-N-formylalanine
methyl ester (.5 mmol, 56.5 mg) were added. The solution was stirred for
either 24 hours with reactions with aldehydes or 48 hours for reactions
with ketones. After the appropriate reaction time, the solvent was
removed from in vacuo and the residue was applied directly to a silica
gel column(4"×75"). Unreactedisocyanide and oxo-compound were eluted with
3:1 hexane:ethyl acetate and the product with 1:1 hexane:ethyl acetate.
Passerini product derived from Boc-Proline, isocyanoacetate derived from
(S)-N-formylalanine methyl ester, and Isobutyraldehyde (Table S1. Entry
3). Mixture of diastereomers and rotamers. Yield: 186 mg (88%). 1H-NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ7.86, 7.31, 6.55, 6.57 (2 H, 4 doublets, J=7.02 Hz),
5.16 (1H, d, J=3.5 Hz), 5.01, 5.07 (1H, 2 doublets, J= 2.6, 4.4 Hz),
4.49-4.64 (2 H, m), 4.34-4.49 (1 H, m), 4.30 (1 H, dd, J=7.8, 5.3 Hz),
3.75, 3.71, 3.70 (6H, 3 singlets), 3.37-3.8 (4H, m), 1.72-2.64 (10 H, m)
1.21-1.47 (24 H, m) 0.80-1.01 (12 H, m); 13C-NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
173.1, 172.7, 171.4, 169.4, 169.3, 80.29, 80.17, 78.4, 77.6, 59.2, 59.0,
52.2, 48.1 48.0 46.8, 46.7, 30.2, 30.1, 30.0, 28.5, 28.3, 24.9, 24.4,
19.2, 18.9, 17.3, 17.2, 16.3, 16.0. HRMS (FAB) calcd for [C19H32N2O7 +
Na]+ 423.2107, found 423.2125.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Investigation of the Configurational Stabilities of Chiral
Isocyanoacetates in Multicomponent Reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
