$DATUM 75-09-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Solvent Procedure Aldehyde 1 (3.0
mmol) and isocyanide 3 (3.3 mmol) were added to the solution of a
carboxylic acid 2 (3.3 mmol) in methylene chloride (3 mL) at room
temperature. The reaction mixture was stirred at ambient temperature for
24 h and then concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was purified by
silica-gel flash chromatography using hexane/ethyl octane 6:4 as an
eluent to afford the corresponding product 4. Compound 4f, yield 88%. 1H
NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 0.89 (t, J= 7.4 Hz, 3H), 1.23 (t, J= 7.1 Hz,
3H), 1.84-2.08 (m. 2H), 2.12 (s, 3H), 3.98 (dd, J= 2.5 Hz, J= 5.1 Hz,
2H), 4.16 (q, J= 7.1 Hz, 2H), 5.07-5.13 (m. 1H), 6.59 (s, 1H). 13C NMR
(50 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 8.9, 14.1, 20.9, 25.0, 40.9, 61.6, 74.7, 169.5,
169.5, 169.8. Anal, calcd. for C10H17NO5: C, 51.94; H, 7.41; N, 6.06.
