$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Ugi Reaction: To a
solution of amine (1.0 mmol) in methanol (2.0 mL) was added aldehyde (1.0
mmol), and the reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 10
min. To this solution was added carboxylic acid (1.0 mmol), and the
reaction mixture was stirred for 5 min, then isonitrile (1.0 mmol) was
added. The resulting mixture was stirred at room temperature until the
reaction was determined to be complete by TLC. The resulting solution was
concentrated in vacuo and purified by silica gel flash column
chromatography (solvents noted) to provide the title compounds.
2-(2-(N-cyclopropylacetamido)-3-methylbutanamido)phenyl 4-cyanobenzoate
(22f): Prepared according to the general procedure from 10f for 15 h to
provide title compound as a white solid (87%) after purification by flash
column chromatography on silica gel, eluting with hexanes to 4:1
hexanes/ethyl acetate gradient. white solid, mp: 117.4-118.6 °C; 1H NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 9.85 (br s, 1H), 8.36 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H), 8.29 (d, J
= 8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.81 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 2H), 7.27-7.21 (m, 1H), 7.12-7.09 (m,
2H), 3.81 (d, J = 10.5 Hz, 1H), 2.74-2.62 (m, 2H), 1.88 (s, 3H), 0.98 (d,
J = 6.3 Hz, 3H), 0.85 (d, J = 6.3 Hz, 3H), 0.99-0.71 (m, 4H); 13C NMR (75
MHz, CDCl3): δ 175.8, 170.3, 163.5, 140.2, 133.5, 132.4, 131.3, 131.2,
127.1, 124.4, 122.4, 122.3, 118.2, 117.1, 73.6, 33.2, 26.6, 23.1, 20.2,
20.1, 10.0, 9.1; IR (film): 3256, 2966, 2873, 2232, 1740, 1691, 1674,
1628, 1608, 1528, 1454, 1390, 1304, 1252, 1174, 1107, 1069 cm-1; MS
(FAB): m/z 420 (M + H).
