$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of the Passerini adducts: general
procedure. The appropriate arylglyoxal or glyoxylamide (1 or 6) (5mmol)
was suspended in diethyl ether (5mL). Acetic acid (3, 5mmol), and the
corresponding isocyanide (2) (5mmol) were successively added, and the
mixture was stirred 48-72 h at room temperature. In the case of using
arylglyoxals (1), an abundant precipitate was formed, which was filtered
and successively washed with i-PrOH and i-Pr2O, yielding a product (4)
usually pure enough to be used in the following reaction. In the case of
using glyoxylamides (6, R1 = NHR or NRR') or glyoxylic esters (6, R1=
OR), the reaction mixture was extracted with CH2Cl2 (4 × 10mL),and the
organic phase was dried with Na2SO4 and concentrated in the rotatory
evaporator. The residue was purified by flash column chromatography(Φ =
3, L = 12cm;hexane/EtOAc from 7:3 to 3:7), giving the corresponding
product (7). In the case of 7e, a precipitate forms, which is filtered,
and washed with i-PrOH and i-Pr2O, yielding the product usually pure
enough to be used in the following reaction. For analytical purposes, the
adducts 4 and 7e were further purified by recrystallisation from ethanol.
Compound 7g, Yield: 87%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Passerini condensation
