$DATUM Isocyanide 3 (3.3 mmol) was added to the suspension of the carboxylic
acid 2 (3.3 mmol) and the aldehyde 1 (3.0 mmol) at room temperature. The
reaction mixture was stirred at ambient temperature for 24 h and then
concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was purified by crystallization
from ethyl octane/ hexane to afford the corresponding product 4. Compound
4a, yield 86%. mp 95-97 °C. 1H NMR (200 MHz. CDCl3): δ = 1.28 (t, J= 7.1
Hz, 3H), 2.19 (s. 3H), 4.06 (d, J= 5.1 Hz. 2H), 4.22 (q, J=7.1 Hz, 2H),
6.13 (s, 1H), 6.72 (s, 1H), 7.33-7.497 (m, 5H). 13C NMR (50 MHz, CDCl3):
δ = 14.7, 21.6, 41.8, 62.3, 75.9, 128.0, 129.3, 129.4, 129.6, 135.8,
168.9, 169.6, 170.0. Anal, calcd. for C14H17NO5: C, 60.21; H, 6.14; N.
5.01. Found: C. 60.14; H, 6.22; N, 5.12, HRMS (ESI): m/z calcd. for
C14H17NO5Na [M + Na]+: 302.1004, Found: 302.0999.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, Passerini reaction, reaction run in solvent gave lower
yield, no solvent
