$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (18) Preparation of Chlorides 1 via Passerini
Reaction To a solution of chloroacetaldehyde (40% soln in H2O, 0.50 mL, 3
mmol) in MeOH (15 mL) was added sequentially acid (3 mmol) and isocyanide
(3 mmol) at r.t. After the reaction was complete at ambient temperature
(monitoring by TLC), the solvent was removed under reduced pressure, and
the residue was recrystallized from Et2O–PE to obtain the chloride 1.
1-(Cyclohexylcarbamoyl)-2-chloroethyl 3-nitrobenzoate (1d): White
crystals, Yield (85%)a mp: 165-166 °C; IR (KBr, cm-1): 3320, 3018, 2936,
2901, 2897, 1721, 1638, 1598, 1332, 1292, 1097, 778; 1H NMR (CDCl3,
600MHz) δ (ppm): 8.91 (s, 1H, Ar-H), 8.51-7.73 (m, 3H, Ar-H), 6.07 (s,
1H, NH), 5.64 (m, J = 4.2 Hz, 1H, COCH), 4.14-3.83 (m, 2H, ClCH2),
3.88-3.83 (m, 1H, NCH), 1.99-1.16 (m, 10H, 5CH2); MS (m/z, %): 354 (M+,
1), 256 (11), 167 (23), 150 (100), 122 (29); Anal.Calcd for C16H19ClN2O5:
C, 54.17; H, 5.40; N, 7.90. Found: C, 54.39; H, 5.73; N, 7.65.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
