$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of
2,3-Dihydro-1H-2-benzazepin-1-ones 8. A mixture of phosphonium salt 3 (1
mmol), amine 5 (1 mmol), isocyanide 6 (1 mmol), and arylglyoxal 4 (1
mmol) was stirred in methanol (5 mL) at room temperature for 24-48 h, and
then the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure. NEt3 (0.20 g, 2
mmol) with toluene (5 mL) was added to the reaction system, and the
reaction mixture was stirred at 110 °C for 2 h. The solvent was removed
under reduced pressure, and the residue was purified by flash
chromatography on silica gel (ether/petroleum ether = 1:4, V/V). 8.
2-Benzyl-4-(4-chlorophenyl)-N-cyclohexyl-2,3-dihydro-1H-2-benzazepin-1-one-3-carboxamide
(8l). White solid (yield 0.41 g, 85%). Mp 237-239 °C; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 600
MHz) δ (ppm) 8.04 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.45-7.14 (m, 12H), 6.91 (s, 1H),
5.40 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 4.95 (d, J = 14.4 Hz, 1H), 4.84 (d, J = 13.8
Hz, 1H), 4.79 (s, 1H), 3.33-3.29 (m, 1H), 1.57-0.50 (m, 10H); 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 150 MHz) δ (ppm) 168.2, 166.5, 141.9, 138.8, 136.8, 134.0, 133.5,
131.4, 131.1, 129.9, 129.1, 129.0, 128.9, 128.8, 128.3, 128.1, 127.1,
62.3, 53.5, 48.1, 32.3, 25.2, 24.5; MS (EI, 70 eV): m/z (%) = 484 (10)
[M+], 358 (98), 268 (32), 91 (100). Anal. Calcd for C30H29ClN2O2: C,
74.29; H, 6.03; N, 5.78. Found: C, 74.56; H, 6.17; N, 5.86.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solvent removed after stage 1, Ugi reaction (stage 1), Wittig reaction
(stage 2)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 2,3-Dihydro-1H-2-benzazepin-1-ones and
3H-2-Benzoxepin-1-ones by Isocyanide-Based Multicomponent Reaction/Wittig
Sequence Starting from Phosphonium Salt Precursors
